$ enola show --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola show [flags] [<revision>] [repo_path|config_path]

Show what one recorded revision did to the architecture.

A revision is a snapshot id or its prefix, a git commit, HEAD~N, @<seq>, a ref
name, or `latest` (the default).

Flags:
  -focus string
    	narrow the delta to entries referencing this module, file or symbol
  -json
    	emit the delta as JSON

Examples:
  # What the latest revision did
  enola show

  # What a past commit did
  enola show HEAD~3

  # Only what touched one module
  enola show --focus internal/auth HEAD~3

See also: enola help log, enola help diff
